  "fill-blanks-cloze": "Trends (2020-2026): Tests vocabulary in context. 2026 trends: Cloze tests requiring knowledge of collocations and appropriate prepositions to maintain the semantic integrity of the passage.",
  "preamble": "Trends (2020-2026): UPSC consistently tests the 'Source' of the Preamble (USA) and the 'Language' (Australia). 2026 NDA I saw a match-the-following on the 42nd Amendment (1976) adding 'Socialist', 'Secular', and 'Integrity'. Conceptual depth: Focus on the Berubari Union case (1960) vs. Kesavananda Bharati case (1973) regarding the Preamble as a part of the Constitution.",
  "schedules": "Trends (2020-2026): High frequency of questions on the 10th Schedule (Anti-Defection Law) and 11th/12th Schedules (Panchayats/Municipalities). 2026 CDS I featured a specific question on the 6th Schedule (Tribal areas in Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura, Mizoram) and the specific powers of Autonomous District Councils.",
  "fundamental-rights": "Trends (2020-2026): Focus on Article 21 (Right to Life) and Article 32 (Writs). 2026 exams emphasized the 'Doctrine of Severability' and 'Doctrine of Eclipse'. Questions frequently test the difference between rights available only to citizens vs. all persons. Article 19(1) sub-clauses are a perennial favorite.",
  "dpsp": "Trends (2020-2026): Shift from direct article-matching to conceptual application. 2026 trends highlight Article 44 (Uniform Civil Code) and Article 50 (Separation of Judiciary from Executive). Fundamental Duties (Article 51A) questions often focus on the 86th Amendment Act (2002) regarding education.",
  "citizenship": "Trends (2020-2026): Focus on the Citizenship Act, 1955 and its amendments (2019). Questions test the modes of acquiring citizenship (Birth, Descent, Registration, Naturalization, Incorporation).",
